List a theme's word lists in order

The games' menu of word lists takes a theme's lists in the order readdir()
gives them, which is the order the disk keeps them in, so that Kidux's
Spanish lists, numbered from the easiest to the hardest, came in any order,
the list with the accents among the first. The theme's lists are now
sorted by their file names, which the theme chooses; the lists all users
share and a child's own still follow them, as they did.

diff --git a/src/titlescreen.c b/src/titlescreen.c
index f2d18e1..a0ed829 100644
--- a/src/titlescreen.c
+++ b/src/titlescreen.c
@@ -1298,8 +1298,24 @@ static int chooseWordlist(void)
   } while (1); /* Loop continues until break occurs */
   closedir(wordsDir);	
 
-  
-  
+  /* The theme's lists in the order of their file names, which a theme */
+  /* chooses, from the easiest to the hardest; readdir() gives them in */
+  /* the order the disk keeps them.                                    */
+  {
+    int i, j;
+    char swap[200];
+    for (i = 1; i < lists; i++)
+      for (j = i; j > 0 && strcmp(wordlistFile[j - 1], wordlistFile[j]) > 0; j--)
+      {
+        strcpy(swap, wordlistFile[j]);
+        strcpy(wordlistFile[j], wordlistFile[j - 1]);
+        strcpy(wordlistFile[j - 1], swap);
+        strcpy(swap, wordlistName[j]);
+        strcpy(wordlistName[j], wordlistName[j - 1]);
+        strcpy(wordlistName[j - 1], swap);
+      }
+  }
+
   /* Adding global custom wordlists ------------------------------------ */
  
   sprintf(wordPath,"%s/words", settings.var_data_path);
